    <div class="tp-tablewrap"><table class="tp-table tp-num"><caption>Common heights in inches</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Height</th><th scope="col">Total inches</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">4 ft 6 in</th><td>54 in</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">4 ft 10 in</th><td>58 in</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">5 ft 0 in</th><td>60 in</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">5 ft 2 in</th><td>62 in</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">5 ft 4 in</th><td>64 in</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">5 ft 6 in</th><td>66 in</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">5 ft 8 in</th><td>68 in</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">5 ft 10 in</th><td>70 in</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">6 ft 0 in</th><td>72 in</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">6 ft 2 in</th><td>74 in</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">6 ft 4 in</th><td>76 in</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">6 ft 6 in</th><td>78 in</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>Health tools and forms often ask for height in inches. For centimeters, use <a href="/feet-to-cm/">feet to cm</a>.</p>
